WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.675
[Nix] ...we seek to do as a firm.

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:11.219
We are a behavior change agency.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.557
The holy grail of communications is

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.726
when you can start to change behavior.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:23.064
Uh, Trinidad. This is a great,
interesting case history

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:24.649
of how we look at problems.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.777
[folk music playing]

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.113
[Nix]
There are two main political parties,

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:32.073
one for the blacks
and one for the Indians.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.159
And you know, they screw each other.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:37.495
So, we were working for the Indians.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:42.417
We went to the client and we said,
"We want to target the youth."

00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:46.796
And we try and increase apathy.

00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:50.341
The campaign had to be non-political,

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.135
because the kids
don't care about politics.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.180
It had to be reactive,
because they're lazy.

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:59.392
So we came up with this campaign,
which was all about:

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:01.603
Be part of the gang. Do something cool.

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:02.854
Be part of a movement.

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.398
And it was called the "Do So!" campaign.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.400
[Kaiser]
It means "I'm not going to vote."

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.319
[Nix] "Do so! Don't vote."

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.404
[crowd cheering]

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.157
[man] The salute of resistance

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:17.160
that is known to all
across Trinidad and Tobago.

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:19.913
Do So! Do So!

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.916
-Do So!
-[crowd continues cheering]

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:26.419
[Nix] It's a sign of resistance against,
not the government,

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:29.005
against politics and voting.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.466
-♪ Run with it, run with it ♪
-♪ Run, run ♪

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:33.134
-♪ Run with it, run with it ♪
-♪ Run, run ♪

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:35.595
[Nix]
They're making their own YouTube videos.

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:39.099
This is the prime minister's house
that's being graffitied.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.934
It was carnage.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:45.480
[Nix]
We knew that when it came to voting,

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:48.608
all the Afro-Caribbean kids wouldn't vote,

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:49.692
because they Do So!

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.404
But all the Indian kids would do
what their parents told them to do,

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:55.240
which is go out and vote.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:57.700
They had a lot of fun doing this,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.829
but they're not gonna go
against their parents' will.

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:02.455
[fireworks crackling]

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.958
[overlapping shouts]

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:09.504
Thank God for the guidance
that has brought us here to this victory.

00:02:09.587 --> 00:02:11.923
Thank you. Thank you, God.

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:17.095
[Nix] And the difference in
18- to 35-year-old turnout was like 40%.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.640
And that swung the election about 6%,

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:23.685
which was all we needed
in an election that's very close.

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:32.610
We now undertake ten national campaigns
for prime minister or president each year.

00:02:33.236 --> 00:02:34.821
Malaysia, we're working in.

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:39.033
[Kaiser] We did Lithuania, Romania,
Kenya, Ghana.

00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:41.536
-[Nix] So quite a few this year.
-[Kaiser] Nigeria.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.081
-[man] The Brexit campaign?
-[Nix] Oh, and the Brexit campaign, yeah.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.333
But we don't talk about that.

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:48.710
[Kaiser] Oops, we won!

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:50.170
[laughter]

